antum_samples) EXCEEDS what's in the scanline, i.e., spp < quantum_samples. \n\nFor LOGL (32844): quantum_samples=1 always. spp forced to 1. Equal. But if we craft header spp with LOGL=2 + alpha, libtiff decode errors BEFORE import. \n\nFor LOGLuv: quantum_samples=3 for spp≠1. Crash when spp=2 (2<3). \n\nSo the target IS LOGLuv spp=2 (alpha). I need a valid SGILOG-encoded 2-sample LOGLuv strip, OR make libtiff decode it. \n\nWait — maybe libtiff's LogLuvDecode handles spp=2 by treating it as... let me just check the libtiff source. Let me find LogLuvDecode in system libtiff.\n</think>The normal decodable files (spp=3 alpha) don't crash since spp==quantum_samples. The crash case is LOGLuv where `samples_per_pixel < quantum_samples` (spp=2 → CIEXYZ reads 3 samples/pixel from a 2-sample buffer). I need a *decodable* 2-sample LOGLuv SGILOG strip. Let me check libtiff's LogLuvDecode to see if spp=2 decodes.\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n"}],"model":"DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731","usage":{"input_tokens":94194,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"274993f6-75dc-41c4-a