ew spp/bps combos with SGILOG compression under ASan to see if any produce a crash directly. Particularly: spp=3 with sf=3 (float) bps=32, LOGLuv SGILOG. And spp=3 with an alpha already. And logl photometric variants. Also spp=4 with bps count handling.\n\nActually the earlier uncompressed matrix gave \"Unknown pseudo-tag 65560\" for spp=1,3,4 meaning GM tried TIFFSetField SGILOGDATAFMT which is only valid for SGILOG compression. That means for photometric LOGLuv, GM ALWAYS sets SGILOGDATAFMT=FLOAT regardless of compression. So even uncompressed LOGLuv hits the FLOAT path! But with uncompressed, the decoder is dumpmode (raw copy), not LogLuvDecode32. So decode copies spp*bps bytes. Then GM import reads quantum_samples.\n\nFor uncompressed LOGLuv spp=3 bps=32 float: scanline=width*12 raw copied. import reads width*3*4. Fine. spp=1: quantum_samples=1, scanline width*4, import reads width*4. Fine. spp=4: quantum_samples=3, scanline=width*16, CompactSamples compacts 4→3 if CONTIG: reads 4 samples/pixel (width*4*4 bytes=64*width? no wait bps=32 so 4 samples*4 bytes=16 bytes/pixel). reads width*16, writes width*12 into same buffer. Then import reads 3 floats. Buffer holds width*16 ≥ width*12. Fine, no overflow. And spp=4 passes Psdif? earlier uncompressed spp=4 gave \"Unknown pseudo-tag\" not Psdif! So spp=4 passes directory read. Good.\n\nSo uncompressed spp=4 LOGLuv: compacted safely, no crash.\n\nHmm. So no obvious crash with these. The alpha-channel angle with spp=4 → quantum_samples=3, compact 4→3, no over-read.\n\nWait — unless the alpha disassociation: after import, if image->matte and alpha_type==AssociatedAlpha, DisassociateAlphaRegion. Not a crash.\n\nLet me reconsider species=4 with SEPARATE planar? quantum_samples=3, spp=4, planar SEPARATE: gate line 1525: planar SEPARATE && quantum_samples!=1 → throw. So blocked.\n\nI keep concluding no crash for clean files. The real vuln likely requires a SPECIFIC crafted combination that the fuzzer found. Given the difficu