{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_fa82fd5f3d1a4c988eea7edbde8380a7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`strip_size_max = TIFFStripSize(tiff)` = rowsperstrip × width × spp × bps/8. For SGILOG float, GM coerces bps=32, `spp=3`, so `strip = width*rowsperstrip*3*4`. Import reads `columns × quantum_samples(3) × 4` per row × rowsperstrip rows = same. Matches. No over-read for spp=3.\n\nI keep confirming: generally the over-read only occurs when `spp < quantum_samples`. Since libtiff forbids spp=2 for SGILOG (the natural CIE Log), perhaps the actual vector is that libtiff *rejects* the extra alpha sample count but GM still processes species differently. \n\nLet me step back and just run the bundled real images (both the logluv and others) plus my variants through a **libFuzzer run with a proper SGILOG seed and enough time**, since the grader's binary is what matters. But system libtiff 4.5.0 differs from bundled 4.0.9.\n\nLet me reconsider whether the grader uses bundled or system libtiff. Let me check the oss-fuzz-build.sh to see how it builds — that reveals the intended configuration.\n\n \n\n \n\n\nLet me check oss-fuzz-build.sh to see the intended libtiff linkage.\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n"}],"model":"DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731","usage":{"input_tokens":93140,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"274993f6-75dc-41c4-a916-f8766775d4e2","uuid":"92d81fff-6d92-40cb-9122-98f7a045fc0a"}
